      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The care that an emergency nurse delivers is critical to the success of treatment of acute headaches. The emergency nurse should obtain a medication history from the patient and offer reassuring information about the relief afforded by prescribed medications and the adverse effects that can occur. Because the best treatment for a patient with recurrent headache syndrome is prevention, the emergency nurse should make sure that appropriate follow-up (e.g., headache specialist or counselor) is arranged before discharge from the emergency department."},
